# Homebrew tap for Geeratya

Generated by `scripts/gen-manifests.sh` in [Aleksanderis/Geeratya](https://github.com/Aleksanderis/Geeratya) for release v@VERSION@; do not edit by hand.

Geeratya is a keyboard-first terminal client for Jira Cloud.

```sh
brew install geeratya/tap/geeratya
```

The formula installs the release archive for macOS on Apple silicon (arm64) and for Linux on x64. The macOS binary is not notarised (at most ad-hoc signed by the linker); installing through Homebrew does not set the quarantine flag, so Gatekeeper does not block it.

Source, docs and issues: https://github.com/Aleksanderis/Geeratya
